"Cross-brand","literature_lens","Sensory marketing works as a perception and behavior lever, especially for abstract attributes such as sophistication and quality.","academic_review","Krishna 2012 - An integrative review of sensory marketing","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1057740811000830","2026-05-25","Review defines sensory marketing as marketing that engages the senses and says it can create subconscious triggers around abstract notions like sophistication or quality.","high","EV-33"
"Cross-brand","strategic_moat","Ambient scent effects are consistently positive and tend to be stronger in service settings than in retail settings.","meta_analysis","Roschk et al. 2016 - Atmospheric effects of music, scent, and color","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022435916300458","2026-05-25","Meta-analysis of 66 studies reports higher pleasure, satisfaction, and behavioral intention when scent is present, with stronger scent effects in service settings than retail.","high","EV-34"
"Cross-brand","product_portfolio","Large assortments can create overload when complexity, task difficulty, uncertainty, and effort-minimizing goals are high.","meta_analysis","Chernev et al. 2015 - Choice overload","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1057740814000916","2026-05-25","Meta-analysis of 99 observations identifies choice set complexity, decision difficulty, preference uncertainty, and decision goal as moderators that make large assortments harder to process.","high","EV-35"
"Cross-brand","product_portfolio","Portfolio breadth can help extension confidence, but only if quality variance stays controlled.","academic_article","Dacin and Smith 1994 - Brand portfolio characteristics","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/002224379403100207","2026-05-25","Findings show a positive relationship between number of affiliated products and favorable extension evaluation when portfolio quality variance is lower.","high","EV-36"
"Cross-brand","price_ladder","Premium and luxury are not binary; consumers perceive an accessible-luxury continuum.","academic_article","De Barnier et al. 2012 - Three levels of luxury","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/bm.2012.11","2026-05-25","Study validates a luxury continuum with accessible, intermediate, and inaccessible levels.","high","EV-37"
"Cross-brand","brand_architecture","Masstige theory explains how premium but attainable brands sit between mass and luxury rather than inside either pole.","literature_review","Paul 2019/2020 - Masstige marketing review","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0148296319305557","2026-05-25","Review differentiates masstige from related constructs and places it in a mass-luxury continuum.","high","EV-38"
"Cross-brand","brand_architecture","Wider availability can grow a luxury-adjacent brand but also reduce distinctiveness and self-differentiation.","academic_article","Atwal et al. 2022 - Luxury democratization","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0148296321007578","2026-05-25","Article conceptualizes democratization of luxury as a perceived reduction in distinctiveness, exclusivity, and self-differentiation due to wider availability and access.","high","EV-39"
"Cross-brand","visual_identity","Premiumness perception is affected by visual design cues including symmetry and dark marks.","open_access_article","Romeo-Arroyo et al. 2023 - Packaging design and premiumness","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1878450X22001913","2026-05-25","Study finds a significant positive effect of symmetry on premiumness perception and frequent association of black marks with premiumness.","high","EV-40"
"Cross-brand","visual_identity","Rarity tends to create stronger luxury value than exclusivity alone, especially for emotional and social value.","open_access_article","Wang et al. 2024 - Rarity and exclusivity in luxury","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/s41262-024-00359-8","2026-05-25","Results show natural rarity positively predicts functional, social, and emotional value, while exclusivity alone did not show significant effects across categories.","high","EV-41"
